+// between a reset and the assert that follows, which is why the digest has been
+// read in fragments across four sessions. Two things are wrong with that pause
+// and neither is only its length. It is a function of the drivers under test:
+// the instrument's readability depends on MetronomeDxe having started, so a run
+// in which it does not would print the 41 copies back to back and lose the
+// digest entirely. And it is 300 ms a copy regardless of what the panel costs to
+// read. A pause that the measurement can change is not part of the instrument.
